# Keep Git's line-ending conversion away from binary payloads.
#
# Git guesses whether a file is text. When it guesses wrong on a compressed
# file and core.autocrlf is on (the Windows default), it rewrites LF bytes
# inside the compressed body. The file still looks like a gzip stream, with
# valid magic bytes and a valid size trailer, but it no longer decompresses.
# A browser fetching it aborts with ERR_CONTENT_DECODING_FAILED and the map
# layer silently fails to load.
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.xls    binary
*.db     binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.tif    binary
*.tiff   binary
*.mp4    binary

# GeoJSON and JSON are text, but they are generated artefacts that should
# round-trip byte for byte, so leave their line endings alone too.
*.geojson -text
*.json    -text
